            <ArticleTitle>Abdominal pain and ketonuria in an 11-year-old girl five months after abdominal trauma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1361-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Five months after an abdominal trauma, a 11-year-old girl was admitted for abdominal pain, hyperglycemia, and ketonuria, which led to the diagnosis of left diaphragmatic rupture with gastric necrosis and perforation. The girl died soon after operation.</AbstractText>
